prompt:
A real photograph of the inside of a small clothes shop in Berlin on a Saturday afternoon, taken as a passer-by would take it with a good phone camera from just inside the door, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus. Natural colours, daylight from the shop window on the right and warm light from the ceiling lamps. The textures of real wood, cotton, wool, denim, leather, fabric and skin.

The first reference picture shows the young woman in three-quarter view, the second from the front: her face, her dark blonde hair tied back in a ponytail, her build and her height stay exactly as in them. Use them for the person only; her clothes here are light-blue jeans, a white T-shirt and a short light-blue denim jacket, with a small brown leather bag on a strap over her shoulder.

THE SHOP is a bright room with pale grey walls and a light wooden floor. Every garment and every object stands on its own, with a little space around it, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. The clothes carry no price tags, no labels and no lettering, and nothing in the shop carries any writing.

The left wall, from the top down:
- a high shelf with a straw hat and a red woollen cap side by side, and two handbags, one black and one brown;
- below it, wooden shelves with neat stacks of folded sweaters in clear colours (yellow, navy blue, grey) and a stack of folded blue jeans;
- at the bottom, a low shelf of shoes in a row: a pair of black leather boots, a pair of white sneakers, a pair of brown sandals and a pair of black leather shoes.

The back of the shop, from the left of the picture to the right:
- a long clothes rail with garments on wooden hangers, each one clearly visible: a red dress, a green skirt, a white shirt, a light-pink blouse, a dark-grey suit jacket with its trousers, a long camel coat and a black leather jacket;
- a fitting room with a dark-green velvet curtain drawn half open, the inside of the cubicle empty, and beside it a tall standing mirror in a wooden frame, turned towards the fitting room, its glass reflecting only the curtain and the pale wall;
- a small wooden stool in front of the mirror.

The right side of the shop:
- a wooden counter with the saleswoman behind it: a woman of about fifty with short dark hair, in a black cardigan, folding a red-and-white striped scarf on the counter; on the counter beside her stands a wicker basket of rolled socks in bright colours, and a pair of brown leather gloves lies next to it;
- on the wall behind the counter, a row of hooks with three leather belts and four ties hanging from them;
- further right, the shop window with daylight, and a tall green plant in a pot on the floor in front of it;
- two round lamps hang from the ceiling.

In the front of the shop, on the left, an older man with grey hair sits on a low upholstered bench, trying on a brown leather shoe; the other shoe of the pair stands on the floor beside his foot.

THE YOUNG WOMAN of the reference pictures stands in the middle of the shop, a little to the right, seen from her head to her shoes, which stand on the wooden floor with their shadow under them. She is caught in the middle of choosing: she holds a yellow sweater up by its shoulders in front of her with both hands, at arm's length, and looks at it with her head tilted, a half-smile that reaches her eyes. She stands upright, her face turned towards the sweater, and the clothes rail and the counter stay visible on either side of her.
